vors passing.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through the twin prisoner's dilemma under evidential decision theory, where my choice is treated as evidence about my twin's choice. I'm setting up the expected utilities for cooperating versus defecting, with p as the chance the twin matches me, and checking when cooperation comes out ahead.\n\nI'm checking the cutoff against the other side of the comparison: the two sides are equal at p = 5/7, which is the same threshold as before. The twins are the same model writing the same essay, so the choice is likely to be correlated; with that correlation above 5/7, the evidential expected value favors passing.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9697,"completion_tokens":641,"total_tokens":10338,"cost":0.051608,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.051608,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.038788,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01282},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":282,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}